## 8) UI + API Endpoints (Minimum)

Teacher pages:
- `GET /teacher/exams/` (single-page filter tool)
- `GET /teacher/exams/<exam_document_id>/` (paper tree)
- `GET /teacher/exams/item/<exam_node_id>/` (item detail)

API endpoints:
- `GET /teacher/exams/api/programs?...` (reuse standards endpoints if possible)
- `GET /teacher/exams/api/courses?...`
- `GET /teacher/exams/api/discover?...` (returns candidate sources)
- `POST /teacher/exams/api/acquire` (kicks off acquisition job)
- `POST /teacher/exams/api/parse` (kicks off parsing job)
- `POST /teacher/exams/api/tag` (kicks off tagging job)
- `GET /teacher/exams/api/results?...` (returns papers + coverage summaries)

Admin endpoints (optional):
- `GET /admin/exams/provenance_report` (CSV/JSON)

---

## 9) Validation Gates (Do Not Skip)

Import/parse must fail if:
- no `source_url` (unless teacher upload)
- missing publisher name
- acquisition_method not in taxonomy
- cannot reproduce a valid exam node tree
- node hierarchy codes do not align with document ordering

Tagging must be marked “needs review” if:
- objective confidence is below threshold
- action verb cannot be mapped to internal taxonomy

---

## 10) Definition of Done (v1)

- Teacher can select a course context and browse at least one past exam down to item level.
- For each exam, the teacher sees provenance: publisher, official link, acquisition method, last verified.
- Items have:
  - objective links (at least 1 per item, with confidence)
  - cognitive level (internal Bloom category)
  - item format metadata
- Mark schemes / scoring guidance are parsed or linked.
- Sample responses are parsed or linked when available.
- The system supports restricted cases via reference-only mode.
